the spring 2022 anime season is coming  to a close with many a surprise both  welcome  and unwelcome  shield hero season 2 proved that the  promise neverland wasn't the only show  that could completely destroy the legacy  built by a great first season with a  gut-wrenchingly miserable second season  but on the other hand kagiasama's third  season rightfully took the throne at the  number one spot on my anime list  until the fullmetal alchemist resistance  force have their say that is proving  that no incredible anime stands a chance  against a good review bombing  and the highly anticipated spy family  yes it is pronounced spy family just how  hunter hunter is pronounced  well hunter hunter  and the highly anticipated spy family  reigns as not only one of the most  highly rated anime of the season but its  most popular as well  it's likely that not a single viewer  here has not seen the show yet or at  least felt the reverberations of its  effects rippling across social media  the numerous positive parts that were  produced out of the show's mass  popularity incredible cosplays fan arts  and such  seem to all be cursed by the law of  equivalent exchange as society's  deviance emerged from the descents of  their delinquency to clamp their claws  upon poor anya the young girl and focus  of much  misconduct  at the hand of the community as was  unfortunately expected to be fair  and if you have not yet witnessed any of  this  frankly  what are you doing  i mean this not to be demeaning nor  interrogative but more so a genuine  question on how you've managed to evade  one of the past couple years most  popular shows yet i suppose if you've  stumbled upon this humble video then you  can no longer make that claim as today i  will dive into not only the origins of  spy family but how it's managed to grasp  the love and admiration of so many souls  within the anime and manga community in  such a short time  come along with me and if you haven't  just watch spy family already  [Music]  tatia endo the creator of spy families  manga began his journey as an assistant  for other rather reputable shonen jump  manga blue exorcist and tatsuki  fujimoto's fire punch  building on this strong foundation and  his tutelage under quite successful  artists upon undertaking his own career  as a mangaka his initial one shots  formed a surprisingly extensive  collection of more mature stories that  stand in stark contrast to the comedic  backdrop of his latest breakout work  despite seeming polar opposites in tone  and topic alike after digging a little  deeper his last three one shots before  beginning spy family most notably  contain clear inspiration actually for  the series  anya's character design quite clearly  originated in the main character of  rengoku no ashey written to be a witch  with pink hair and horn-shaped ornaments  adorning her head  likewise endo claims that ishini usubeni  tatsuni hoshi was the first work to  inspire him to draw a small child's  character  which was very far out of his comfort  zone as a primarily seinen and dark  mangaka making him attribute this work  specifically to the reason he was even  able to write a young character like  anya in the first place later on  his last work before spy family i spy is  i mean i'm sure you can tell the  similarities here  upon the suggestion of his editor after  combining the best parts of these three  one shots and imbuing them with the  comedic basis that was missing from all  of his previous works something that the  editor believed could really turn around  the popularity of his writing endo  created spy family a series whose  initial reception among the editorial  department was supposedly so good that  its serialization was practically  decided before any proposals or meetings  were even extended an auspicious  foreboding for what was to come since  debuting in 2019 spy family has risen to  critical acclaim and cemented its place  in shonen jumps top 10 best-selling  manga in both years since  and it's safe to say that wit studio and  cloverworks adaptation of its anime is  following in the footsteps of that giant  but now that i've finished that chapter  of the lore it raises the question of  just what exactly elevates it to that  level  looking once again at the best-selling  shonen jump manga of last year spy  family is almost nothing alike its high  rolling compatriots  shonen jump has been experiencing a  transition into darker series for the  past couple years illustrated by the  front runner of the pack jujutsu kaisen  and the rising popularity of the work of  his former mentor tatsuki fujimoto's  huge cult-hit chainsaw man  spy family a romantic charming and  endearing comedy stands alone as a black  sheep  but perhaps that's exactly why it's so  great  spy family revolves around a spy named  twilight who must infiltrate into a  foreign country find a prominent yet  secretive politician and gather  intelligence on him in order to maintain  the safety of the entire world however  the only public outings this politician  attends to are at his son's school  exclusive to society's elite forcing  twilight to enlist the help of a young  girl anya and woman yore to act as his  pretend daughter and wife in order to  invade the politicians close circle  through this school and complete his  very dire mission  however unbeknownst to twilight the  seemingly tame civil servant yore  moonlights as an underground assassin  known as the thorn princess and the  strangely perceptive anya happens to be  an esper who can read minds  and this three-prong dynamic is the  source of the humor throughout spy  family as twilight yore and anja hide  their identities from each other  however anya actually knows from the  start exactly what everyone is hiding by  well reading their minds  because of this anya is arguably the  most fundamental factor that spy  families plot  story and comedy hinges upon restating  the importance of the character that  tatia endo has been crafting throughout  his works purposefully or not over the  span of almost the last decade of his  career  us viewers experience this family  vicariously through anya as she is aware  of other characters thoughts plans  things that normally only we would have  access to forming the dramatic irony of  the story  she shares those feelings with us  except through the special lens of a  child  more so than being jokingly manipulative  it is actually endearing to watch her  take advantage of her father's need to  complete his mission and obligation to  do anything for her to make sure she  does well in school  in moments of fear her cries to her mom  come across not as genuine panic for the  viewer but rather joy in seeing her  dependence on her mother who can and  will  annihilate anyone  the very serious jobs of spy and  assassin are twisted into the  perspective of a six-year-old child we  get to enjoy what anya sees as a  childlike fantasy rather than the  objectively strange and  quite precarious situation that it  really is  but interspersed among these moments of  hilarity  shine moments of real insight into the  heart of family as well  though twilight yore and anja are  created to be very different characters  defined by their rather extreme traits  or occupations they share one main  similarity  that they are alone  twilight lives a life of deception and  impermanence moving from mission to  mission and reminding himself to remain  detached always  yor though she has a brother is forced  to live a life of secrecy and crime for  the sake of both their well-being and to  maintain the facade on the outside  so as to not be suspected for her double  life  and anya a child out of a decrepit  orphanage and result of human  experimentation  has never had a real family  underneath this surface the comedy masks  the story of three lost souls finding  solace in one another  what initially begins as a strictly  professional agreement slowly develops  into a heartwarming realization of the  comfort that genuine relationships can  have for any of us  so whether you're watching spy family  for this or the humor or the occasional  action  it's a great show regardless  as always this has been the anime  culture corner i hope you enjoyed the  video don't forget to like and subscribe  for future in-depth show manga and  character analyses  you
 

